From: duck-brain <duck-brain@localhost>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 22:56:56 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] duck-brain P22: --dry-run, and torque off when robotd stops
 or the bus goes silent

Alex's answers of 07.11.2026, before the first stand-up on the duck:
- robotd --dry-run (Feetech only, needs --journal): the servos and the
  IMU are read, the loop, the ramp and the policy run, the targets go to
  the tick journal - and nothing is written to the bus: no torque, no
  goal, no P/D. robot.health -> feetech.dry_run.
- Stopping takes torque off every servo: the Feetech driver's Drop runs
  at the end of the loop (Ctrl+C, SIGTERM) and while a panic unwinds;
  only when this run switched torque on, never in a dry run.
- A bus where no servo answers for 5 ticks with torque on: three
  unverified writes of 40 = 0, health degraded (feetech.silent_cutoff);
  once servos answer again the cut is repeated, verified, for those that
  heard none of it. Back with robot.relax, then init, as after the
  undervoltage cutoff.
